= Architecture =

BITwiki is a MediaWiki-based semantic knowledge and memory system. V2 favors native MediaWiki primitives over filesystem-like organization.

== Structural rule ==
'''Namespace ≠ entity type ≠ domain ≠ scope ≠ Book Matter ≠ epistemic status.'''

Each describes a different dimension of knowledge.

== Page anatomy ==
A page may contain:

* namespace — its system role;
* entity type — what kind of thing it describes;
* one or more domains — fields of knowledge it belongs to;
* optional scope — a real contextual boundary when one exists;
* semantic relationships — how it connects to other knowledge;
* Book Matter — its reusable content sections;
* epistemic metadata — how claims are sourced and qualified.

== Navigation ==
Portals, indexes, category trees, semantic queries, and graphs are views over the underlying knowledge model. Navigation must not become the ontology itself.

== Modularity ==
Pages should remain coherent canonical knowledge objects while important semantic portions can be addressed and transcluded independently. V2 does not require every section to become a separate page.

== Minimal semantics ==
The semantic model should begin small and expand only when actual content requires new properties, entity types, or relationships.

